<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $L: \calX \rightarrow \calX ''$ be a left adjoint to the inclusion, let $S$ be the collection of all monomorphisms $u$ in $\calX $ such that $Lu$ is an equivalence, and let $\calX ' = S^{-1} \calX $ be the collection of $S$-local objects of $\calX $. Since $L$ is left exact, $S$ is stable under pullbacks and therefore determines a topological localization of $\calX $. By construction, we have $\calX '' \subseteq \calX '$. The restriction $L| \calX '$ exhibits $\calX ''$ as an accessible left exact localization of $\calX '$. Let $u$ be a monomorphism in $\calX '$ such that $Lu$ is an equivalence. Then $u$ is a monomorphism in $\calX $, so that $u \in S$. Since $\calX '$ consists of $S$-local objects, we conclude that $u$ is an equivalence. It follows that $\calX ''$ is a cotopological localization of $\calX '$, as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>